## Algorithm
1. Start.
2. Create an AVL tree by inserting nodes.
3. Calculate the height and balance factor of each node.
4. Search for the node to be deleted.
5. If the node has exactly one child, replace the node with its child.
6. Update the height of the affected nodes.
7. Calculate the balance factor using:
   Balance Factor = Height of Left Subtree − Height of Right Subtree
8. If the balance factor becomes greater than 1 or less than −1, perform the appropriate AVL rotation.
9. Continue updating the heights and balance factors up to the root.
10. Display the updated AVL tree using inorder traversal.
11. Stop.
